## Intent & Decisions
User asked for deep research on blog posts about implicit state machines, to ground a new cs-review perspective that finds implicit state machines that should be explicit. User approved the agent's proposed source set ("start with your suggestions, I can adjust later").
Settled: new agent state-machine-reviewer, primary sources Wlaschin "Designing with types: Making state explicit" and Khourshid "The FaceTime Bug and the Dangers of Implicit State Machines"; supporting sources Minsky, Pocock, Dodds, Khourshid (disabling a button), Harper, King, Sachs, Clayton, DevIQ, Biffle, Hobden, statecharts.dev, Misamore, Wayne. Rules S1-S11 plus a "When not to flag" section built on Wlaschin's "when not to use this approach" and Clayton/Sachs limits. Proposed explicit form is a pure transition function returning next state plus effect description, so it agrees with fcis-reviewer. Minor bump 0.31.0 -> 0.32.0.

